      {
        "id": 95650,
        "name": "Edwin",
        "username": "Edwin",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/73ab20/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-15T15:48:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Volcano's should change your mind on this very quickly. Gazelle has so much great suportt and Enviro Allies is incredible in all of the harder environments like Atlantis and Rook City.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I remain unconvinced that Atlantis is hard.&nbsp; I've won all but one of my games there.&nbsp; I can see the potential for it to interact disastrously with Omnitron et al, but I've not seen it happen in actual play yet.&nbsp; Final Wasteland is the Environment where I've NEVER lost a game (I even added Iron Legacy to my list of victims last night - he was the first villain in one of my games who actually got removed from the game by Unforgiving Wasteland, though the Chupacabras did kill my other two heroes before Nightmist became invincible - fortunately no UW in play at that point, and Setback's mostly-useless incap ability was key to keeping the Mongolian Death Worm coming back to eat Angry Paul's face for about six turns running), and I certainly can see having fun with these Naturalist cards there, but in most cases, I'd be very hesitant to allow the Environment to run unchecked, in case something nukes Environmental Allies or Gazelle Form at an inconvenient time - if you've been letting the Krakens or Dinosaurs get into play in large numbers, and suddenly they stop being harmless…</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
