      {
        "id": 95651,
        "name": "Ameena",
        "username": "Ameena",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-03-15T22:13:11.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Heh, try fighting the Matriarch in Atlantis, wait for Mystical Defences to come out when there's a bunch of Fowl in play and you have no soak, and then see what happens ;).</p>\n<p>If you're fighting someone who can nuke your ongoings then yes, of course you have to be careful of letting the environment get too much stuff out…but that's always a risk when fighting someone who can break your stuff. But as long as it's not something like Devastating Aurora or Sedative Flechettes, which nuke <span class=\"bbcode-i\">all</span> your ongoings, hopefully you and the other heroes can get out enough stuff between you that you can ditch thatinstead of Environmental Allies and Gazelle Form if those are really keeping you going at that time. Actually even Gazelle Form wouldn't matter so much if it gets nuked on the villain turn, because the environment won't get a chance to do anything before you have your turn and just stick it right back into play again on your Power phase :D.</p>",
